# The trial of pod-quic in podnet: podnet moves from quinn 0.11 to noq 1.4
# through pod-quic. src/warp/quic.rs keeps endpoint and client_config and
# takes pod-quic's QueuedDatagrams over a Link of the stack's UdpConn (its
# WarpUdpSocket, SendPoller and SendReady, with their two tests, leave
# podnet). Each other user of quinn (src/cloudflare/{mod,quic,rpc}.rs,
# src/proxy.rs, src/tunnel.rs, src/warp/{h3,l4,session}.rs, src/ws.rs)
# names noq; the endpoints that quinn made with ring's keys
# (Endpoint::client, Endpoint::server, ServerConfig::with_crypto) are
# pod-quic's (endpoint::bind, endpoint::server, endpoint::server_config).
# Each podcrates tag moves to the tag of the hand-off. The record, the size
# and the layers of the files, the build, the bans and the sources of
# cargo-deny, clippy, the tests of the library (the edge over QUIC, MASQUE
# over HTTP/3, the L4 proxy and the WARP session on loopback servers of
# noq), the integration tests of the edge, TLS, the doctor and the API, the
# fuzz targets with their lock, rustfmt, each Rust toolchain of the
# workflows and build images against the rust-version of podcrates, and the
# binary for x86_64 musl, built with zig (a debug build: the release
# profile takes LTO), with podnet's static check of it.
cargo run -q -p podnet-todo -- remap Cargo.lock > /dev/null
cargo run -q -p podnet-todo -- check
python3 scripts/check-size.py
python3 scripts/check-layers.py
cargo build -q
command -v cargo-deny > /dev/null || cargo install -q --locked cargo-deny
cargo deny --locked check bans sources
! cargo tree -q -e normal -i quinn 2> /dev/null
cargo clippy -q --all-targets -p podnet -p podnet-netns -p podnet-core -- -D warnings
cargo test -q -p podnet --lib
cargo test -q -p podnet --test egress --test tls --test doctor --test api_surface --test cli
cargo update -q -w --manifest-path fuzz/Cargo.toml
cargo check -q --manifest-path fuzz/Cargo.toml --bins
cargo fmt --all --check
python3 -I "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-consumer-toolchains.py"
cargo zigbuild -q --target x86_64-unknown-linux-musl -p podnet --bin podnet
sh scripts/check-static.sh "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/debug/podnet"
